    "text1":  [
                  "This loop is a full-value Wellington region bikepacking ride that starts and finishes in Petone, combining multiple sections of the Remutaka Great Ride with a return leg back to the harbour.",
                  "Expect a broad mix of terrain: mostly easy-rolling river trail, historic rail-trail climbing over the Remutaka Incline, quiet lake-edge roads, and exposed coastal stretches where conditions can shift quickly."  
                  
              ],
    "text2":   "Distance and total climbing are substantial for a weekend mission, so most riders will enjoy this as a 2-3 day trip rather than a rushed overnighter. <br> Featherston is the main service and overnight hub on the eastern side, and planning food, water and transport options in advance makes the ride far more relaxed.",
    "text3":  "The Wild Coast is an exposed Grade 3–4 backcountry section. Check current trail conditions and the weather before leaving Featherston. Expect loose rock, sand, stream crossings and limited services.<br>Make sure your lights are charged as the Summit Tunnel is over 500m long and very dark!"
,
